; The canonical change from S4 to S5.
;
; S4 |- S5. Strata compiles Strata.
;
; Strata has no primitives: data, definitions, application, `let` and `match`,
; and nothing else. That is what makes a compiler for it writable in it. It is
; also what stops the compiler resolving its own names -- there is no equality
; to compare two names with -- so the compiler takes a resolved core in which
; a variable is an index, a constructor is a tag and an arity, and a
; definition is a position. Resolving is the reader's job.
;
; The target has structured control flow, as Wasm does. What the compiler does
; is linearise a tree of expressions into a sequence of stack instructions,
; turn application spines into explicit pushes and applies, and turn pattern
; matching into a tag dispatch that binds its fields by position.
;
; The bootstrap is the ordinary one, and it is the acceptance of the layer:
; the compiler's own source compiled by the reference evaluator, and that
; compiled compiler run on the same source, are the same.
(change
  (kind foundation)
  (name "S4->S5")
  (predecessor (foundation-of "foundations/S4"))
  (delta-meta (file "changes/S4-S5/delta-meta.canon"))
  (delta-grammar (file "changes/S4-S5/delta-grammar.canon"))
  (feature
    (feature
      (name "the self-hosting compiler")
      (programs [
        (file "features/strata/compile.generated.meta")
      ])
      (sources [
        (text-file "features/strata/compile.meta")
        (text-file "strata/compiler/compile.strata")
      ]))))
